&gt; Want to shape the future of frontier AI auditing? At AI Verification and Evaluation Research Institute (<https://www.averi.org/|AVERI>), we conduct ambitious pilot audits like this, carry out technical and policy research to inform audit design, and turn what we learn into better tools, standards, and policy for the emerging field of frontier AI auditing. Join us. We are currently hiring for two roles. Apply by September 9th.
&gt; 
&gt; 
&gt; 1. *<https://www.averi.org/careers?ashby_jid=cee7cad4-1da2-4fc0-b185-987b08833079.|Security Research Engineer>*
&gt; 
&gt; AVERI is looking for a Security Research Engineer to lead and execute on cyber risk strategy. This role involves a mix of ensuring the security of AVERI’s pilots, informing secure practices across the frontier audit ecosystem, and contributing cybersecurity risk expertise on pilots.
&gt; Salary range: $220,000-$330,000USD
&gt; 
&gt; *<https://www.averi.org/careers?ashby_jid=22ea26f6-6c8b-449d-9f82-706ea0858eda|2. Project Manager, Pilot Audits>*
&gt; 
&gt; AVERI is hiring a Project Manager with AI auditing and assessment experience to serve as the operational backbone of our pilot audit program. This role will coordinate audit engagements end to end, manage timelines and deliverables and contribute directly to audit fieldwork and reporting.
&gt; Salary range: $155,000-240,000 USD

CAIS is hiring (note: internship applications close 8/31)!

&gt; The Center for AI Safety is hiring!
&gt; 
&gt; Research Engineer / Research Scientist: You’ll conduct empirical research on frontier AI systems: design experiments, train and evaluate at scale on our compute cluster, and publish at top venues.
&gt; 
&gt; Research Manager: You are a senior researcher who can unblock hard technical problems, manage the team's performance, and translate strategic direction into day-to-day priorities. Not sure you count as a "manager"? Apply anyway. We weight research ability most heavily and would rather grow a great researcher into the manager role.
&gt; 
&gt; Research Interns (Fall): Our Ph.D. and undergraduate interns work alongside our researchers, often lead their own projects, and first-author the resulting papers. Applications close August 31.
&gt; 
&gt; Apply: <https://safe.ai/careers|safe.ai/careers>

